      "type": "Feature",
      "properties": {
        "image": "photos/IMG_5049.jpeg",
        "caption": "Mt. Washington Summit! Three-quarters of the way to the end, the White Mountain Range rises up to greatly reduce daily mileage from 20+ miles a day to 10-12 miles. While extremely beautiful and unique, the landscape is amazing during nice weather. However, the worst weather in the world has been recorded atop Mt. Washington, and storms form quickly and hit hard. We ended up hiking another three days on the exposed ridge in the White in pouring rain and 40+ mph winds. The worst weather we experienced on the trail.   ",
        "marker": "Markers/Mountain.svg",
        "alt": "Kasey in front of Mt Washington sign during foggy weather."
